WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:02.620
I pay a lot of attention
to what's going on

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.730
in environmental sustainability.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:06.160
In most of the places that we live,

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.210
if you wanna reflect back 10 or 15 years,

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.810
the climate literally is changing.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.136
There is no planet B!

00:00:12.136 --> 00:00:13.760
And I believe that my kids,

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.690
when they are adults and when
they are actually at a point

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.840
in their career where they
can make a difference,

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.333
it will be too late to
have made a difference.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:24.020
For Ryan Popple, business is personal.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.220
Regardless of where you work,

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.380
I think you've gotta be
asking tough questions

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.930
about what are we going to do

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.800
to actually solve this problem?

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.900
The co-founder and executive director

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.880
of EV startup, Proterra,
is determined to usher

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.300
in the age of clean energy.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.000
The technologies are now largely

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.700
in place to solve the climate crisis.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.170
And for his part, he's
focused his crosshairs

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.340
on a sometimes overlooked contributor

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.147
of carbon emissions, buses.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.100
Buses and freight trucks
combined, comprise about 30%

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.490
of the world's carbon emissions

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.920
from the transportation sector.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.340
Replacing internal combustion
buses with eBuses is well

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.520
in the works and electric buses are poised

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.800
to take over half the
world's bus fleet by 2025,

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.860
but there is one problem.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.993
Almost all of them are in China.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.700
As of 2019, China had
already amassed a fleet

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.010
of over 420,000 electric buses.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:37.390
Europe was at just over 2,000.
The United States about 600.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.700
Today, electric buses
make up less than .1%

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.200
of America's public transportation fleet.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.677
So now we gotta ask ourselves,
"Well, if China was able

00:01:45.677 --> 00:01:50.437
"to get it done, and eliminate
200,000 barrels of oil

00:01:50.437 --> 00:01:53.607
"per day by switching their
bus fleets to electric,

00:01:53.607 --> 00:01:55.590
"then we oughta be able
to get it done as well."

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.940
The problem though is

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.980
that we will not see the
political will or consensus

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.070
in the United States or
Europe to quickly move away

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.700
from fossil fuels to clean technology.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.920
The good news is that

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.310
while diesel buses have
been getting more expensive,

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:14.860
3 to 4% per year, electric
buses keep getting cheaper

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:15.900
and they keep getting better

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.040
and they're a much better user experience.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.520
We wanna win using market forces

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.160
and be completely independent,

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.460
whichever way the political
winds are blowing.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:28.070
After college, I served in the US Army

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.590
and that's really what transformed my view

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:31.953
around energy security.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.490
Just seeing how volatile
some parts of the world are,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.960
in particular parts that
we're very much dependent

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.093
on for fuel production
or petroleum supply.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:49.220
Every day the world needs about
100 million barrels of oil

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.730
and so that is absolutely
an unsustainable situation.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.010
The answer to energy security is going

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:57.170
to be finding alternatives to petroleum.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:00.320
It's not going to be trying
to produce more petroleum.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.490
After his tour of duty,

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.030
Ryan went to business school
and landed himself a job

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.773
at Tesla in its early years.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.380
My reason for being at Tesla was not

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.880
because I was a sports car enthusiast.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.670
It was because of the clean
tech aspect of what Tesla did.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:19.160
You cannot solve the
congestion problem simply

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.950
by making cars cleaner.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.680
A big piece of the sustainability story

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.880
around Proterra is the
benefit of mass transit.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.840
This was a way to get clean EV technology

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.960
into the absolute mass market,

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.880
right now, and not wait for
electric cars to be cheap enough

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.030
for everyone in the
economy to afford them.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.270
Today, Ryan heads the charge

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:45.930
for zero emission battery-electric
buses in North America.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:47.750
Manufacturing its own vehicles

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.270
in facilities in California
and South Carolina,

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.000
Proterra has sold over 900 electric buses

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.060
to transit agencies
throughout the US and Canada.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:59.250
Based on the promise of lower
operating costs and less noise

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.160
and pollution than diesel buses,

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.860
the company says its city
bus can go about 350 miles

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.340
on a single charge,
over twice the distance

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:10.470
of an average city bus's daily mileage.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.640
Throughout the EV world,

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.810
the best products are
going to be those products

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.630
that were purpose-built and designed

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:18.710
from scratch to be an electric vehicle.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.750
We make our own chargers.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.610
We make our own battery
modules. We make our own packs.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.870
We vertically integrate into
any technology where we find

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.553
that the existing supply
chain isn't good enough

00:04:29.553 --> 00:04:30.820
for where we're trying to go

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.447
from a performance-based system.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.700
To make the cost-benefit more attractive

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.360
to local deficit hawks,

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.310
Proterra has innovated a
battery-leasing program,

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:43.170
allowing cities to go electric
at the same price point

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.453
as a standard diesel.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:47.010
When you buy a diesel bus,

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.620
you don't pay upfront for
12 years of diesel fuel.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.550
That would be hundreds
of thousands of dollars

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:53.930
of capital expenditure.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:57.260
So what we do is, we break
the battery out of the cost

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:00.210
of the vehicle and then they
pay for the battery over time,

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.380
like it was the fuel.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.750
And that's enabled a lot of cities

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:04.800
that might not necessarily
have the capital

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.283
to make the switch, to
be able to do so now.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.660
Proterra is already
moving beyond city buses

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.490
to electrify other
types of large vehicles.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:15.910
They've recently begun
delivering electric school buses

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.630
with its partner Thomas Built Buses.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.170
The company has secured over $500 million

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.690
in private investment to date,

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.450
much of it from major auto makers,

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.400
which seems to vindicate
Ryan's pro-business approach

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.930
to sustainability.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.250
Technologically,

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.530
we are at the moment

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.130
where we can start really
scaling clean energy.

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:37.270
Solar, wind, energy
storage, energy efficiency,

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.470
electric vehicles, charging stations,

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:42.790
these are the high-growth
industries in the 21st century.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:46.210
If investors can make
better returns investing

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.600
in clean energy technology,

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.330
then it really doesn't matter whether

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.420
or not you convince anyone
that it's the right thing

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.970
to do or the wrong thing to do.

